{"kind":"propose","text":"Adopt the scope for closing the approved-but-never-landed gap found in audit e2699f17. Ratification adopts the scope for a design note and its implementation requests; it authorizes no code by itself.\n\n1. MAKE THE MERGE HOLD STRUCTURAL. A request that withholds landing says so in a body field (landing=held), not in prose. The fold projects a held commitment with a live approved reporting artifact as awaiting-authorization, waiting on the requester, because the release is the requester's move. A ratified structured merge authorization (the existing authorizes_candidate report) moves it to awaiting-merge, waiting on the performer. Only the sealed merge receipt, or an explicit supersession that states abandonment, closes it. Requester ratification of an explicit report cannot mark a held commitment satisfied. The release step thereby appears in waiting_on_you and cannot be forgotten.\n\n2. ONE COMPLETION PER PROMISE. When a promise already carries a live reporting artifact, an explicit report without body.verdict on the same promise is refused unless it carries body.resolution=no-merge with a reason. Today the newest explicit report silently overrides the artifact and hides the awaiting-merge state; that is the exact move in #15164.\n\n3. RETIRING AN APPROVED HEAD NAMES ITS DISPOSITION. Superseding a request whose commitment has a live approved reporting artifact is admitted only when the successor request rests on that artifact (carried) or the act declares body.disposition=abandoned. Abandoned approved heads become a queryable set instead of vanishing as cancelled rows.\n\n4. LANDING JOIN IN THE PROJECTION. Extend the merged-head reconciliation design (30768e3f5a, itself approved and unlanded) to the opposite direction: every commitment whose completion or approval names a reviewed head that is not an ancestor of the integration head shows not_landed, gs work and MCP work gain an approved_not_landed lane, gs status prints its count, and /v0/worktrees marks each branch approved, landed, or neither. This alone would have shown every item in the audit.\n\n5. DISCIPLINE. AGENTS.md step 5 and SKILL.md name the owner of a hold: the requester who withholds a merge owns its release or its explicit abandonment; \"completed without merging\" is not a closure. The planner loop reads the approved_not_landed lane each tick. Each unmerged worktree must map to an open lane row; otherwise it is deleted.\n\n6. RECOVERY. Recut on current main, with fresh artifacts, review, and structured authorization, in this order: the outcome map (hugh's authorization #14837 stands), the SKILL.md MCP-install pointer, the thread-actions and merged-head reconciliation and retirement-succession design notes, the config cross-process CAS repair, the staleness-cause rows, and the decision-records UI loop. Classify and delete the remaining unmerged worktrees.","body":{"stale_bases":"git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:e2699f1768ec99e886fa58960b2bf4afd1fd4831 stale; retired bases: git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:0e74c3f618a3083014fbbf48216f0bfb3a3d35ea, git:sha1:5d2622748872b7e2dec3fe5c59e4be73a35e0bc8#git:sha1:991e53132b819b1a0c90b8eb04c3f40630863279"}}